2. **Increased Pressure**: To overcome the increased resistance caused by increased viscosity, the pressure difference between the arterial and venous compartments must also increase. This means that the pressure at the arterial end of the capillaries will need to be higher, and the pressure at the venous end will need to be lower to maintain the flow.

