   a. Increased cell proliferation: Oncogenes can promote cell division by promoting the activation of cell cycle proteins, such as Myc, which activates the transcription of genes that promote cell division.

   b.Reduced cell death: Oncogenes can inhibit the process of apoptosis, which is the programmed removal of damaged or damaged cells. This can help to prevent the death of cancer cells, leading to their proliferation and survival.

