6. Nanostructure engineering: Develop new synthesis methods to create zeolites with specific nanostructures, such as hierarchical structures, core-shell structures, or core-shell-shell structures. These nanostructures can lead to improved performance in various applications.

7. Computational modeling: Use computational modeling to predict the properties of zeolites and guide the design of new zeolites with desired properties. This can help reduce the time and cost associated with experimental synthesis.

8. Scale-up and sustainability: Develop scalable and sustainable synthesis methods that can be used to produce zeolites on an industrial scale. This includes using renewable precursors, reducing waste, and optimizing the production process for energy efficiency.

