","To calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction, we can use the following formula:

ΔH_reaction = Σ ΔH_f(products) - Σ ΔH_f(reactants)

where ΔH_reaction is the standard enthalpy change of the reaction, and ΔH_f(products) and ΔH_f(reactants) are the standard enthalpies of formation of the products and reactants, respectively.

For the given reaction:

CaO(s) + H2O(l) → Ca(OH)2(s)

