   H2O(l) + 3/2 O2(g) → H2O(l) (not useful for this calculation)

Now, we need to find the combustion reaction for ethanoic acid (CH3COOH):

4. Combustion of ethanoic acid (CH3COOH):
   CH3COOH(l) + 3/2 O2(g) → CO2(g) + 3H2O(l)

