\]  
(b) The integral of $3 e^{x}$ is $3 e^{x}$, and the integral of $2 \sqrt{x} = 2 x^{1/2}$ is $2 \cdot \frac{x^{3/2}}{3/2} = \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2}$.  
Thus,  
\[
\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = \left[ 3 e^{x} + \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2} \right]_{0}^{1} = 3 e^{1} + \frac{4}{3} (1)^{3/2} - (3 e^{0} + \frac{4}{3} (0)^{3/2}) = 3 e + \frac{4}{3} - 3 = 3 e - \frac{5}{3}.
