Using the identities $\cos \left( \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha \right) = -\sin \alpha$, $\sin (-\pi - \alpha) = -\sin (\pi + \alpha) = \sin \alpha$, $\cos \left( \frac{11 \pi}{2} - \alpha \right) = \cos \left( 5\pi + \frac{\pi}{2} - \alpha \right) = \cos \left( \pi + \frac{\pi}{2} - \alpha \right) = -\cos \left( \frac{\pi}{2} - \alpha \right) = -\cos \alpha$, and $\sin \left( \frac{11 \pi}{2} + \alpha \right) = \sin \left( 5\pi + \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha \right) = \sin \left( \pi + \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha \right) = -\sin \left( \frac{\pi}{2} + \alpha \right) = \cos \alpha$, the expression simplifies to:
