","Let $M_n$ be the amount of millet in the feeder after the $n$-th replenishment, and $S_n$ be the amount of other seeds in the feeder after the $n$-th replenishment. The total amount of seeds in the feeder after the $n$-th replenishment is $2n$ halves of a quart, so $2n$ quarters of a gallon.

On Monday, the initial amount of seeds is $\frac{1}{2}$ quart, and $40\%$ is millet, so $M_0 = \frac{1}{2} \times 0.4 = 0.2$ and $S_0 = \frac{1}{2} \times 0.6 = 0.3$.

After Monday, the total amount of seeds is $\frac{1}{2}$ quart. The mice consume $30\%$ of the millet and $90\%$ of the other seeds. The remaining amount of millet is $0.2 \times (1 - 0.3) = 0.2 \times 0.7 = 0.14$, and the remaining amount of other seeds is $0.3 \times (1 - 0.9) = 0.3 \times 0.1 = 0.03$.

On Tuesday, Miley adds $\frac{1}{2}$ quart of the same blend, so $0.25$ millet and $0.125$ other seeds. The total amount of millet is $0.14 + 0.25 = 0.39$, and the total amount of other seeds is $0.03 + 0.125 = 0.155$. The total amount of seeds is $0.39 + 0.155 = 0.545$. The proportion of millet is $\frac{0.39}{0.545} \approx 0.715$.

