1. The incident electron energy \( E_0 \) is small compared to the Fermi energy \( E_F \), i.e., \( E_0 \ll E_F \).
2. The plason energy \( E_p \) is also small compared to \( E_F \), i.e., \( E_p \ll E_F \).
3. The plasson energy \( E_p \) is much larger than the electron energy \( E_0 \), i.e., \( E_p \gg E_0 \).

