   - Moles of acetic acid (CH₃COOH): 0.333
   - Moles of ethyl alcohol (C₂H₅OH): 1 (since 1 gram-mole of acetic acid is present, and 0.333 moles remain, the reaction consumes 1 - 0.333 = 0.667 moles of ethanol.)
