     \[
     D_{kl} = \sum_{mn} \Sigma_{klmn} E_{mn}
     \]
   - The conductivity tensor \( \Sigma_{ij} \) is defined as:
     \[
     D_{i} = \sum_{j} \sigma_{ij} E_{j}
     \]
   - This can be written in index notation as:
     \[
     D_{i} = \sum_{j} \sigma_{ij} E_{j}
     \]
   - The conductivity tensor \( \sigma_{ij} \) is the inverse of the conductivity tensor \( \sigma_{ij} \), i.e., \( \mathbf{D} = \sigma \mathbf{E} \).

2. **Transformation to New Coordinates**:
